---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Reach from '../components/Reach.astro';
import { pick } from '../data/faq';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Guide
  page="privacy"
  lede="Cupola has no server, so your data has nowhere else to go. It talks straight to your services, keeps their keys on your device, and contacts only two other hosts, each for one reason."
  questions={pick('leaves', 'certs', 'account')}
  related={['install', 'faq', 'contribute']}
>
  <div class="not-prose"><Reach /></div>

  <h2>Nothing collected</h2>
  <p>No sign-up, no analytics, no crash reports. Your services keep their own logins.</p>

  <h2>The two other hosts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong><code>image.tmdb.org</code></strong> for posters and cast photos, because that is where Seerr points. No credentials are sent, but TMDB sees your IP address.</li>
    <li><strong><code>plex.tv</code></strong>, once, if you sign in to Seerr with Plex. Cupola does not keep the token.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Everything else comes from your own servers.</p>

  <h2>Keys stay on your device</h2>
  <p>API keys, tokens and passwords live in the Keychain on Apple devices and in the Keystore on Android. A Seerr invite shares the server's address, never its key. Moving to a new phone is encrypted and stays on your Wi-Fi.</p>

  <h2>Self-signed certificates</h2>
  <p>Cupola asks before trusting a certificate it has not seen, then pins it to that host. Services behind the same proxy are trusted together. Review or remove them in <strong>Settings › Security › Trusted certificates</strong>.</p>

  <h2>Away from home</h2>
  <p>A connection can have a second address for when you are out, through your VPN or reverse proxy. Cupola never sends a key over plain <code>http</code> across the internet. Cloudflare Access, proxy passwords and custom headers are supported.</p>

  <h2>Background search is off by default</h2>
  <p>A search that keeps running after you leave the screen hands the request, key included, to the operating system. That is why it starts off. Tasks expire after 11 minutes, and finished ones are cleared at every launch.</p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>No cookies, and fonts served from this site. Visits are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and does not track you across sites.</p>

  <p>All of the certificate handling is in one file you can read in the <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/lib/core/network/cert_trust.dart`} rel="noopener">source</a>.</p>
</Guide>

<style>
  .not-prose {
    width: min(var(--well), calc(100vw - 2 * var(--gutter)));
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
</style>
